---
title: Do we need a licence to launch a business credit card in four markets?
subtitle: Legal research memo for the co-founders. Placeholder positions, not legal advice.
---

## Answer {#answer}

Whether we need a licence depends on the market. The UK, Germany and France all require a licence or authorisation. Spain needs no licence if we issue the card through a partner bank. Spain is also the fastest to launch, at 2 months, and Germany the slowest, at 6 to 9 months.

These are placeholder positions for testing the memo, not legal advice. They come from one source for all four markets.

